    "created_at": "2021-01-20T14:28:55Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-01-20T14:28:55Z",
    "body": "I'm for making the implementation simpler, and I would be ok with further changes to the \"rendered legend\" to that end, e.g. as suggested here: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/3094#issuecomment-434200972\r\n\r\n(That is, only the first-child-of-type `legend` element in a `fieldset` can be the \"rendered legend\", and some styles turn off the legend magic (without causing another element to become the \"rendered legend\").)\r\n\r\nOne design consideration however is that I wanted a `legend` element that is *not* a child of a `fieldset` to have no special treatment, so that it can be reused in the future together with a new element. Would it be OK to only blockify `legend` elements that are children of a `fieldset`?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
