    "created_at": "2021-01-24T11:30:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-01-24T11:30:13Z",
    "body": "> I think it'd be better if the HTML spec was changed to say that all legends are blockified at computed-value time\r\n\r\nI disagree. I think a `<legend style=\"display:inline\">` that **isn't** the rendered legend of a fieldset should create an inline box, not a block. Making a blockification decision at box construction time works fine and wasn't particularly hard to implement. I think the current spec is easier and more predictable for authors since `display` works normally on `<legend>` when it's not a rendered legend.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
